# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit the filled-in file — .env is gitignored.
# On the Pi:  cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# IMPORTANT: Docker's env_file parser does not strip trailing comments. Everything
# after the "=" becomes the value, "# like this" included. Keep every comment on
# its own line, and put nothing after a value.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# Two independent model roles, both required for every question. Anthropic has
# no embeddings endpoint, so the embedding role necessarily uses a different
# vendor — a real constraint, not an oversight.

# Embedding role: embeds the question so it can be matched against the index.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Generation role: writes the grounded answer.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- model roles -------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave commented out to use the defaults in config.py. The index records which
# embedding model built it and the app refuses to query an index built with a
# different one, so changing this means re-running ingest.py.
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# Generation role. Default is claude-haiku-4-5 ($1/$5 per MTok) rather than
# claude-opus-5 ($5/$25): this step is constrained extraction from a supplied
# evidence block, not open-ended reasoning. Measured on this corpus a query is
# ~4k input + ~700 output tokens, so ~$0.0075 against ~$0.0375 — 5x cheaper.
# Raise it per-run for a harder question; the model used is recorded in the run
# record either way.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# --- local generation, no API key, no spend -----------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama runs generation against a local Ollama server instead of
# a hosted API. It is a documented FALLBACK, not the recommended default.
#
# Measured on a Raspberry Pi 5: ~8 tokens/second, so a full answer takes about
# 70-90 seconds, and a 26B model will not fit in available RAM. More seriously,
# a small model tends not to hold the grounding contract — in testing,
# qwen2.5-coder:1.5b returned schema-valid JSON and fluent prose that cited no
# evidence handle at all. Validation now rejects that (`ungrounded_answer`),
# which is the correct outcome and also means the local path will often produce
# a recorded failure rather than an answer.
#
# Use it to demonstrate the pipeline with no credentials, not to get good answers.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:1.5b
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=300
# OLLAMA_NUM_PREDICT=1200

# --- where the service listens ON THE HOST -----------------------------------
# The Pi's side of the port mapping, not the container's.
#
#   127.0.0.1  loopback only (default). Reach it with an SSH tunnel —
#                ssh -L 8501:127.0.0.1:8501 pi@raspberrypi
#              — or over Tailscale. Nothing is exposed to your LAN.
#   0.0.0.0    reachable from any device on your LAN. Convenient, and it means
#              anyone on the network can spend your API budget.
#
# Do not port-forward this to the internet without authentication in front of
# it — see docs/deployment/raspberry-pi.md.
BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
HOST_PORT=8501

# --- host settings -----------------------------------------------------------
TZ=Europe/London
